  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 at 48.5% accuracy), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries any discriminative signal for this task. The very low baseline suggests either the task is inherently difficult or PCA on 2000 dims is an inadequate representation. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the simplest image-only configuration: it tests a fundamentally different information source (visual cellular morphology via a pretrained deep encoder) against the RNA-only baseline. This single experiment answers the highest-level design question—does the image modality provide useful signal at all?—before committing budget to the 30+ multimodal or more complex RNA-encoder variants. If image_only performs substantially better, it justifies investing in multimodal fusion and ViT variants; if it performs similarly poorly, the search should focus on improving RNA representations (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation. This is the most informative single experiment because it partitions the remaining configuration space into two very different strategic directions."
}

